## On the Open Problems

**`green_38.lower`:** Asks whether ∃ c > C₁ ≈ 3.2578 with (fun n ↦ c^n) =O[atTop] ans and ans ≤ᶠ[atTop] LargestAdmissibleCardinality. This asks to improve the lower bound beyond 367^{1/5}.

**`green_38.upper`:** Asks whether ∃ c < C₂ ≈ 3.3177 with ans =O[atTop] (fun n ↦ c^n) and LargestAdmissibleCardinality ≤ᶠ[atTop] ans. This asks to improve the upper bound below 7cos(π/7)/(1+cos(π/7)).

Both ask to narrow the gap [3.2578, 3.3177] for Θ(C₇). This is a genuinely open problem. The Shannon capacity Θ(C₇) is known only to lie in this interval. Determining whether Θ(C₇) = ϑ(C₇) = C₂ (as is the case for C₅ where Θ(C₅) = √5 = ϑ(C₅)), or whether the true value is strictly less, remains unresolved despite decades of work.

